# {{dist}}

A [Shape](https://github.com/sqllocks/shape) plugin for the `{{group}}` group (it implements the
`{{protocol}}` protocol of plugin API v1). Written by `shape plugins new {{dist}} --group {{group}}`.

## Layout

- `src/{{package}}/__init__.py`: the plugin (`{{class}}`) and `SHAPE_API`, the plugin API version it
  was written for.
- `tests/test_conformance.py`: runs the Shape plugin conformance kit on it.
- `pyproject.toml`: the entry point that makes Shape find the plugin.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: runs the tests and the kit on every push and pull request.

## Try it

```bash
pip install -e . pytest
pytest
python -m shape.plugins.kit {{dist}}
shape plugins info {{group}}:{{name}}
```

The generated plugin is a working skeleton that does the least that conforms. Replace the body of
`{{class}}`, keep the tests passing, and add tests for what it really does: the kit checks that a
plugin follows the rules of the API, not that it is correct.

